dence_ids":["link.euler.proposition-2.8"],"id":"euler.proposition-2.8","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 2.8","locator":"Proposition 2.8, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 2.8.** Assume (2.7), let $\\mathbf a$ be the amplitude vector of Lemma 2.6, with the couplings of Lemma 2.7, and suppose that $0<\\varepsilon_+\\le\\varepsilon/32$ and $T\\ge2(\\varepsilon\\varepsilon_+)^{-1/2}$. Then the interval $\\tau_m\\le\\tau\\le2(\\varepsilon\\varepsilon_+)^{-1/2}$, where $\\tau_m\\ge2/\\varepsilon$ is the zero of $Y$ (Lemma 2.5), contains a crossing. At every crossing in this interval the strength $\\sigma_+=|\\mathbf a(\\tau)||k(\\tau)|$ satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n C^{-1}(\\varepsilon\\varepsilon_+)^{-1/2}\n \\le\\frac{\\sigma_+}{\\lambda\\max_{[0,T]}|\\mathbf a|}\n \\le C(\\varepsilon\\varepsilon_+)^{-1/2}. \\tag{2.23}\n\\end{equation}$$ Moreover $$\\begin{equation}\n |\\mathbf a(\\tau)|\\le\\exp\\bigl(3-\\varepsilon^{-1/2}\\bigr)\n \\max_{[0,T]}|\\mathbf a|\\qquad(0\\le\\tau\\le1). \\tag{2.24}\n\\end{equation}$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.proposition-2.8","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.proposition-2.8","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-2.8%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-2.8%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.4"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.proposition-2.8","id":"sha256:db